// The points-to stage, coarse: what Argus.Analysis.Extraction runs when
// even the bounded stage (points_to_bounded.dl) outgrows its budget. The
// same program, held to the same budget, with every leaf resolved by the
// coarse pass (clientlib/pervasive.dl), pervasive or not. The bounded
// stage outgrows its budget where the program's terms merge into each
// other, each holding every other's fields (ex_mcp's client and transport
// states, through the helpers both hand them to), whatever leaves they
// hold; the coarse pass follows the leaves alone, a row per source a leaf
// reaches, so its rows grow with the sources and the leaves, never with
// the terms. It writes the same relations, points_to_mode saying
// "coarse", and every leaf as resolved coarsely (pervasive.csv).

.include "points_to.dl"

stage_mode("bounded").
stage_mode("coarse").
